															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sad-boi-hours" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4914832); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4914832&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834599" alt="Sad Boi Hours" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4914832)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sad-boi-hours" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4914832); return false;" >Sad Boi Hours</a></span> <span class="odate time_1553075017 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Mar 2019 09:43</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4190976">
									

<p>Honestly, first impressions, are pretty decent!</p>
<p>You've stuck to the standard format, you've maintained an acceptable clinical tone throughout, and you have a decent bit of science stuff to keep me interested (i love science!)</p>
<p>My main issue here is that the idea isn't that interesting. This can work so much better by giving us some sort of narrative flow aside from the experiment logs. this, right now, is a magic item which does a magic thing which would've <em>thrived</em> in series I.</p>
<p>You could've added something like:</p>
<p>On [Insert date], SCP-XXXX was recovered in [location], alongside a journal written by [person]. The journal can be found below.</p>
<p>You could've pulled the &quot;crazy science man who defies all logical laws by creating something which defies logic and does it whilst not believing in himself&quot; trope. Let's say that this man who has created this SCP is suffering from low self-esteem and mental illness which feeds into the creation of the SCP.</p>
<p>by making the creator of the SCP suffer from a problem which nearly everyone has struggled with, he becomes more relatable. He's just a man who wanted to do something great with his life but didn't believe in himself and got killed by his own creation.</p>
<p>In your journal for this character, you could include self-deprecating insults to make him more relatable. Put emphasis on these insults and as each journal page (collapsible?) progresses, you can put emphasis on him descending into insanity as he breaks all laws of science by creating this SCP?</p>
<p>If you want examples of good narrative flow, you can check:</p>
<p><a href="/scp-4205">SCP-4205</a><br />
<a href="/scp-087">SCP-087</a><br />
<a href="/your-very-first-scp">Your Very First SCP!</a></p>
<p>Happy writing, my man! For a first SCP, this is excellent work! It's just that you need a solid idea and a good narrative flow!</p>

							</div>

								
					
